  ],
  "body": [
    "Our passionate, inspiring and dedicated team members deliver impact where it matters – and have fun doing it. Together, we work to create a more just and equitable world through fairer trade practices.",
    "We envision a world in which justice and sustainable development are interwoven with trade and business, one where every person can maintain a decent, dignified livelihood. Fairness, integrity and transparency are core to everything we do at Fairtrade.",
    "If you share this vision - join us.",
    "We are Hiring!",
    "Senior Business Development Manager: The Senior Business Development Manager’s primary responsibility is to increase licensing revenue and expand the commodity portfolio by creating and maintaining strong relationships with prospective commercial partners across branded and retail opportunities. This person will drive the strategy for new revenue growth through commercial partnerships, communication of the Fairtrade value proposition, and creative paths to partnership to encourage certification and grow market access for Fairtrade producers in the US.",
    "Follow us on LinkedIn for the most up-to-date information on upcoming positions and news throughout the year. Looking forward to connecting with you!",
    "Optimism Optimism We recognize the reality of unjust systems and also see the possibilities in the problems we confront every day. We pursue our work with a dogged belief that we can and must contribute to a better future.",
    "Sustainability Sustainability As individuals and as an organization, we are committed to making decisions today that support a vibrant future. We prioritize taking care of ourselves and our teams so that we have the verve to do the work ahead. We work towards long-term solutions that build generational security and foster environmental resilience.",
    "Curiosity Curiosity We leverage the intersection of our wonder and humility to further the Fairtrade mission. We believe that taking calculated risks is an essential part of personal and organizational growth. By intentionally creating a culture where failing forward is welcome, we give ourselves space to ask big questions, try new things and learn from our collective experiences.",
    "Trust Trust We have confidence in the talents, efforts and intentions of each member of our team. We foster an environment of integrity through honest and transparent collaboration both as thoughtful leaders and active followers.",
    "Empathy Empathy We believe in showing up for people where they are—from holding space for another to providing tangible support. We leverage our seat of power in the US to actively include producers where decisions are being made about them without them. Whatever form it takes, we’re committed to functionally honoring the dignity of all people.",
    "Excellence Excellence Excellence in our work is both the means and the ends in our pursuit of improving farmer livelihoods. We approach our work with a collective determination to raise the bar and encourage each other to push past roadblocks. As a result of this mentality we foster innovation, deliver tangible results and establish ourselves as a world-class partner uniquely positioned to create change.",
    "Fairtrade America recognizes that being inclusive is about action. Therefore, we are not only advocating for justice, equality and non-discrimination for farmers and workers in low- and middle-income countries, but also within our own organization and with commercial partners, governments and the communities where Fairtrade products are produced and purchased.",
    "Fairtrade America is committed to an inclusive and diverse workforce. We do not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, color, national origin, religion, age, sex or gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or pregnancy-related conditions), gender identity or expression (including transgender status), marital status, sexual orientation, physical or mental disability, genetic information, military service or veteran status, or any other status protected by law."
  ],
